{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that repairs Java 8 code so that it correctly solves the given programming problem. The code reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Repair the following Java 8 code so that it correctly solves the programming problem. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your repaired code should implement the problem correctly, meaning that it should produce the correct output for any valid input.\nPrint your repaired code and also the confidence score you give to your repair. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<repaired_code>\n<your_repaired_code>\n</repaired_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the problem description:\n<problem_description>\nFirecrackers scare Nian the monster, but they're wayyyyy too noisy! Maybe fireworks make a nice complement.Little Tommy is watching a firework show. As circular shapes spread across the sky, a splendid view unfolds on the night of Lunar New Year's eve.A wonder strikes Tommy. How many regions are formed by the circles on the sky? We consider the sky as a flat plane. A region is a connected part of the plane with positive area, whose bound consists of parts of bounds of the circles and is a curve or several curves without self-intersections, and that does not contain any curve other than its boundaries. Note that exactly one of the regions extends infinitely.\n</problem_description>\n\nHere is the Java 8 code you have to repair:\n<original_code>\nimport java.io.*;\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        new Main().go();\n    }\n\n    void go() {\n        try (BufferedReader br = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n             BufferedWriter bw = new BufferedWriter(new OutputStreamWriter(System.out))) {\n            \n            int id = 1;\n            String line;\n            while ((line = br.readLine()) != null) {\n                String[] tokens = line.trim().split(\"\\\\s+\");\n                if (tokens.length < 2) continue;\n                \n                int n = Integer.parseInt(tokens[0]);\n                int D = Integer.parseInt(tokens[1]);\n                if (n == 0 && D == 0) break;\n                \n                bw.write(\"@\" + id++ + \"\\n\");\n                \n                final double R = 1;\n                Point left = new Point(-D, 0);\n                Point right = new Point(D, 0);\n                \n                for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n                    line = br.readLine();\n                    tokens = line.trim().split(\"\\\\s+\");\n                    int sl = Integer.parseInt(tokens[0]);\n                    int sr = Integer.parseInt(tokens[1]);\n                    double vLeft = sl * Math.PI * R / 180.0;\n                    double vRight = sr * Math.PI * R / 180.0;\n                    int t = Integer.parseInt(tokens[2]);\n                    \n                    if (sl == sr) {\n                        Point shift = right.minus(left).rotate(Math.PI / 2).unit().multiply((vLeft + vRight) * 0.5 * t);\n                        left = left.plus(shift);\n                        right = right.plus(shift);\n                        continue;\n                    }\n                    \n                    double x = D * (vLeft + vRight) / (vLeft - vRight);\n                    Point center = left.plus(right).multiply(0.5);\n                    Point pivot = center.plus(right.minus(center).unit().multiply(x));\n                    \n                    Point lVec = left.minus(pivot);\n                    Point rVec = right.minus(pivot);\n                    double wLeft = vLeft / lVec.norm();\n                    double wRight = vRight / rVec.norm();\n                    \n                    lVec = lVec.rotate(wLeft * t);\n                    rVec = rVec.rotate(wRight * t);\n                    \n                    left = lVec.plus(pivot);\n                    right = rVec.plus(pivot);\n                }\n                \n                Point mid = left.plus(right).multiply(0.5);\n                bw.write(String.format(\"%.10f\\n\", mid.x));\n                bw.write(String.format(\"%.10f\\n\", mid.y));\n                bw.flush();\n            }\n        } catch (IOException e) {\n            throw new RuntimeException(e);\n        }\n    }\n\n    static class Point {\n        double x, y;\n\n        Point(double x, double y) {\n            this.x = x;\n            this.y = y;\n        }\n\n        Point plus(Point p) { return new Point(x + p.x, y + p.y); }\n        Point minus(Point p) { return new Point(x - p.x, y - p.y); }\n        \n        Point rotate(double theta) {\n            double c = Math.cos(theta), s = Math.sin(theta);\n            return new Point(x * c - y * s, x * s + y * c);\n        }\n        \n        Point unit() {\n            double len = norm();\n            return multiply(1.0 / len);\n        }\n        \n        Point multiply(double k) { return new Point(k * x, k * y); }\n        \n        double norm() { return Math.sqrt(x * x + y * y); }\n    }\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<repaired_code>\nimport java.io.*;\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        new Main().go();\n    }\n\n    void go() {\n        try (BufferedReader br = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n             BufferedWriter bw = new BufferedWriter(new OutputStreamWriter(System.out))) {\n            \n            int id = 1;\n            String line;\n            while ((line = br.readLine()) != null) {\n                String[] tokens = line.trim().split(\"\\\\s+\");\n                